<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōlŏquĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n.
		proloquor. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An introduction</i>, <i>preamble</i>,
			Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 226</span></i> Müll.; v.
			prologium.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An assertion</i>, <i>proposition</i>,
				<i>axiom</i> (class. Lat. pronunciatum), the Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξίωμα</span>, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 16,
				8, 1</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p.
				29, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disjunctivum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					5, 11, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A judicial sentence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub uno proloquio cunctos jubet occidi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">28, 1, 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
